---
// Real draft flagged for attorney review (compliance.md rule 5). A2P 10DLC
// required elements per compliance.md rule 9: SMS program description,
// opt-out instructions, message/data-rate disclosures, carrier liability
// disclaimer, 18+ age restriction. Also carries this surface's one instance
// of the third-party disclosure (rule 3 — footer/about/terms/best-of guide)
// and the one-to-one TCPA consent architecture (rule 2).
import BaseLayout from "../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../../lib/site-config";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../../lib/schema";

const lastUpdated = "August 16, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of Service | ${site.brandName}`}
  description={`Terms of service for ${site.brandName}, including our SMS messaging program terms.`}
  quoteHref="/contact/#lead-form"
>
  <Fragment slot="schema">
    <script
      type="application/ld+json"
      set:html={JSON.stringify(
        breadcrumbSchema([
          { name: "Home", url: `https://${site.domain}/` },
          { name: "Terms of Service", url: `https://${site.domain}/terms/` },
        ])
      )}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-content max-w-3xl">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-fluid-sm text-muted mb-4">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-caliche-dark hover:underline">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
        <span>Terms of Service</span>
      </nav>

      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-fluid-3xl">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fluid-sm text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="card-rail bg-sand p-5 mt-8 mb-8">
        <p class="text-fluid-sm text-muted">
          <strong class="text-ink">Draft notice:</strong> these terms are a good-faith working
          draft and are flagged for review by a licensed Arizona attorney before or within 30 days
          of this site's public launch, per this business's standard compliance practice. They are
          not themselves legal advice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-content max-w-none">
        <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
        <p>
          By using {site.domain} (the "Site"), operated by {site.legalDisclaimerName} ("we," "us,"
          "our"), you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please do not use the
          Site.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What this Site is — and isn't</h2>
        <p>{site.disclosure}</p>
        <p>
          We are not a contractor, and we do not perform fencing or block wall installation or
          repair work. Any statements about pricing, licensing, or code requirements on this Site
          are provided for general informational purposes and are not a substitute for a
          contractor's own written quote or a licensed attorney's advice on your specific situation.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Eligibility — 18+ only</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old to submit a quote request or opt in to SMS
          communications through this Site. By submitting a request, you represent that you are 18
          or older and have the authority to request services for the property described.
        </p>

        <h2>4. SMS messaging program terms</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Program description:</strong> if you opt in via the checkbox on our quote request
          form, {site.legalDisclaimerName} may send you text messages related to your specific
          quote request — including confirmation, status updates, and messages from the independent
          contractor(s) matched to your project. This is a transactional messaging program tied to
          your request, not a general marketing list.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Consent scope (one-to-one):</strong> your SMS consent names the specific
          business(es) authorized to text you — {site.legalDisclaimerName} and the independent
          contractor(s) matched to your submitted project. If your project is later referred to a
          different provider than the one named at submission, we obtain that provider's own
          consent from you before they send any automated marketing message. Consent is never
          required to submit a quote request — the SMS checkbox is optional, and unchecking it does
          not prevent us from processing your request by phone or email.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Message frequency:</strong> may vary based on your request and any follow-up
          needed to connect you with a contractor.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Message and data rates may apply.</strong> Standard rates from your wireless
          carrier apply to any messages sent or received.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Opt-out:</strong> reply <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to a message from us to
          opt out of further SMS communication. You may also contact us directly through our
          <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Help:</strong> reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message for assistance, or
          contact us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Carrier liability disclaimer:</strong> carriers are not liable for delayed or
          undelivered messages. Message delivery is subject to effective transmission from your
          network operator and depends on factors outside our control, including your device and
          service coverage.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Supported carriers:</strong> most major U.S. wireless carriers are supported;
          coverage may vary.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Call recording</h2>
        <p>
          Calls to our tracked phone number may be recorded, consistent with Arizona's one-party
          consent law (A.R.S. § 13-3005, § 13-3012(9)). See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy
          Policy</a> for more detail.
        </p>

        <h2>6. No guarantee of licensing, insurance, or workmanship</h2>
        <p>
          {site.licensedInsuredHedge}. We do our best to match requests to businesses that report
          appropriate Arizona ROC licensing, but we do not independently verify every contractor's
          license, insurance, or workmanship on an ongoing basis, and we make no warranty —
          express or implied — regarding any contractor's work. You are responsible for your own
          diligence, including verifying license status at roc.az.gov, before hiring anyone.
        </p>

        <h2>7. No fee to homeowners</h2>
        <p>
          Requesting a quote through this Site is free for homeowners and property owners. We do
          not charge you for matching you with a contractor.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.legalDisclaimerName} is not liable for any
          damages, disputes, or losses arising from your interactions with, or the work performed
          by, any independent contractor matched through this Site. Your relationship with any
          contractor you engage is solely between you and that contractor.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The content on this Site — including text, cost guides, and design — is owned by
          {site.legalDisclaimerName} or its licensors and may not be copied or reproduced without
          permission, except as needed for your own personal, non-commercial reference.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this
          page reflects the most recent revision. Continued use of the Site after changes take
          effect constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Arizona, without regard to its
          conflict-of-law principles.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Reach us via our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
